## Context
helptext.go holds a `helpText` map with all command help strings. The doc
comments on each `cmd*` function repeat the same content. Two sources of
truth for the same information; changing a command's help requires editing
two files.

The root cause: ticket 0089 enriched doc comments, ticket 0090 added runtime
help strings — neither reconciled with the other.

## Actions
1. In each command file (validate.go, check.go, close.go, etc.), define a
   package-level `const helpXxx = \`...\`` holding the full help text.
   Remove the duplicate rule list from the `cmd*` doc comment; replace with
   a one-liner referencing the const.
2. Rewrite helptext.go as a thin registry:
   ```go
   var helpText = map[string]string{
       "validate": helpValidate,
       "check":    helpCheck,
       ...
   }
   ```
   commandOrder stays in helptext.go — it is cross-cutting, not per-command.
3. Verify erg validate --help and erg --help --all still produce correct output.
4. make test passes.

## Drift bugs fixed during the refactor
While moving content, reconcile two pre-existing drifts between helpText and
cmd* doc comments:

- cmdLog doc said the actor-verb log-line format was "not enforced"; helpText
  said "enforced by erg validate (rule 11)". The helpText wording is correct
  (rule 11 in validate.go enforces LogLineRE). Keep the helpText wording.
- cmdMigrate doc said "Exits 1 on archive/→closed/ filename collision";
  helpText said "Always exits 0". migrate.go (around line 129) returns 1 on
  collision — the doc comment is correct. Update helpMigrate to match the
  doc-comment wording.

## Verification
Baseline help output (build/erg --help=all plus per-command --help) must
match byte-for-byte after the refactor except for the helpMigrate exit-code
sentence (the deliberate fix above).

## Exit criteria
- Each command's help string is defined once, in the same file as its cmd* function.
- helptext.go contains only the registry map and commandOrder.
- No duplicate rule lists between helptext.go and command file doc comments.
- The two drift bugs (helpLog, helpMigrate) are reconciled.
- make test passes.
